      "content": "Subject: Ensuring Ergonomic Workstations for Optimal Health and Productivity\n\nDear Team,\n\nAs we continue to embrace the flexibility of remote work, it's essential to ensure that our workspaces are conducive to both productivity and health. To that end, I would like to share some important ergonomic guidelines to help you set up your desks to avoid wrist or back pain from prolonged sitting.\n\n1. **Chair and Desk Height**: Your chair should support your lower back and allow your feet to rest flat on the floor or on a footrest. The desk height should enable your forearms to be parallel to the floor when typing, with your wrists straight and your elbows at a 90-degree angle.\n\n2. **Monitor Placement**: Position your monitor at eye level, about an arm's length away, to avoid straining your neck. Consider using a monitor stand or adjustable arm if necessary.\n\n3. **Keyboard and Mouse Position**: Place your keyboard and mouse close enough to prevent overreaching. Your wrists should remain straight and your hands should be in a neutral position while typing.\n\n4. **Frequent Breaks**: Take regular breaks to stretch and move around. This helps to alleviate muscle tension and prevent repetitive strain injuries.\n\n5. **Erg",
